      ":question/id": "aab65aed-48d5-5bce-ba06-7c3e6ee06314",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Simplify $\\cos(x-225^\\circ)$ using $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$. Enter signed coefficients.\n\n{{field-1}} $\\sin x+$ {{field-2}} $\\cos x$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use $\\cos(u-v)=\\cos u\\cos v+\\sin u\\sin v$ with $u=x$ and $v=225^\\circ$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos(x-225^\\circ)&=\\cos x\\cos 225^\\circ+\\sin x\\sin 225^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\cos x\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)+\\sin x\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sin x-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first blank is $- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ and the second is $- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.",
